sequenceDiagram
    participant "Hangfire Scheduler" as HangfireScheduler
    actor "DormantUserPurgeJob" as DormantUserPurgeJob
    actor "UserRepository" as UserRepository
    participant "PostgreSQL Database" as PostgreSQLDatabase
    participant "AccountDeletionService" as AccountDeletionService
    participant "AuditLogService" as AuditLogService
    participant "OperationalLogService" as OperationalLogService

    activate DormantUserPurgeJob
    HangfireScheduler->>DormantUserPurgeJob: 1. Execute Monthly Purge Job
    DormantUserPurgeJob->>OperationalLogService: 2. Log job start
    activate UserRepository
    DormantUserPurgeJob->>UserRepository: 3. FindDormantUserIds(dormancyThreshold)
    UserRepository-->>DormantUserPurgeJob: List<Guid> userIds
    activate PostgreSQLDatabase
    UserRepository->>PostgreSQLDatabase: 4. SELECT UserId FROM Users WHERE LastLoginDate < @threshold
    PostgreSQLDatabase-->>UserRepository: Row set of UserIds
    DormantUserPurgeJob->>DormantUserPurgeJob: 5. Loop: For each userId in userIds
    DormantUserPurgeJob->>AccountDeletionService: 5.1. Enqueue account deletion job
    AccountDeletionService-->>DormantUserPurgeJob: string jobId
    DormantUserPurgeJob->>OperationalLogService: 6. Log job completion
    activate AccountDeletionService
    HangfireScheduler->>AccountDeletionService: 7. Process Deletion Job
    activate AuditLogService
    AccountDeletionService->>AuditLogService: 8. Create audit record for deletion request
    AccountDeletionService->>UserRepository: 9. HardDeleteUser(userId)
    UserRepository->>PostgreSQLDatabase: 10. BEGIN; DELETE FROM ... WHERE UserId=@userId; COMMIT;
    PostgreSQLDatabase-->>UserRepository: Transaction status
    AccountDeletionService->>OperationalLogService: 11. Log successful deletion

    note over AccountDeletionService: This flow reuses the exact same permanent account deletion logic as the user-initiated flow, ensu...
    note over AuditLogService: The audit log must be written to an immutable, WORM-compliant storage (e.g., S3 with Object Lock ...

    deactivate AuditLogService
    deactivate AccountDeletionService
    deactivate PostgreSQLDatabase
    deactivate UserRepository
    deactivate DormantUserPurgeJob
